2) b. Write a HTML program, to explain the working of tables by preparing a timetable. (Note: Use
<caption> tag to set the caption to the table & also use cell spacing, cell padding, border, rowspan,
colspan etc.).
<!DOCTYPE html>
<head>
<title>Timetable Example</title>
<style>
table {
border-collapse: collapse;
width: 80%;
margin: 20px auto;
font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
border: 2px solid #444;
}
th,
td {
border: 1px solid #333;
padding: 15px;
text-align: center;
}
th {
background-color: #f0f0f0;
}
caption {
font-size: 1.5em;
margin-bottom: 10px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1 style="text-align: center;">Weekly Timetable</h1>
<table cellspacing="5" cellpadding="5">
HTML (LAB)
<caption>Class Schedule</caption>
<!-- Table Header -->
<tr>
<th>Day</th>
<th>9:00 AM - 10:00 AM</th>
<th>10:00 AM - 11:00 AM</th>
<th>11:00 AM - 12:00 PM</th>
<th>Break</th>
<th>1:00 PM - 2:00 PM</th>
<th>2:00 PM - 3:00 PM</th>
</tr>
<!-- Monday -->
<tr>
<td>Monday</td>
<td>Math</td>
<td>Science</td>
<td rowspan="2">Lab</td>
<td rowspan="5">Lunch</td>
<td>History</td>
<td>Geography</td>
</tr>
<!-- Tuesday -->
<tr>
<td>Tuesday</td>
<td>English</td>
<td>Physics</td>
<td>Chemistry</td>
<td>Sports</td>
</tr>

<!-- Wednesday -->
<tr>
<td>Wednesday</td>
<td>Biology</td>
<td>Math</td>
<td>Computer Science</td>
<td>Art</td>
<td>Music</td>
</tr>
<!-- Thursday -->
<tr>
<td>Thursday</td>
<td>Chemistry</td>
<td>English</td>
<td>Physics</td>
<td>History</td>
<td>Drama</td>
</tr>
<!-- Friday -->
<tr>
<td>Friday</td>
<td>Math</td>
<td>Biology</td>
<td>Geography</td>
<td>Computer Science</td>
<td>Sports</td>
</tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
